  "decision": {
    "row": 149,
    "source_reading": "Theorem 4.3, first bullet, unrestricted converse on the entire subdifferential domain is refuted by the proper convex extended-real counterexample. Its subdifferential domain misses the finite midpoint even though all pairs satisfy the modulus-two bound.",
    "corrected_reading": "On a convex V contained in the global subdifferential domain, strong interpolation and strong monotonicity for all choices of global subgradients are equivalent, with the original norm and nonnegative modulus.",
